{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Before the face of the Master, HaShem.</b> Three festivals there are at three seasons: the festival of Pesach is the season of spring, the festival of Shavuot is the season of the harvest, and the festival of Sukkot is the season of the ingathering; and all three are appointed times concerning the grain and all the plants of the earth. And we are obligated in them to give thanks to HaShem, for He is good, and to appear in them before the face of the Master, HaShem, who sustains His servants and nourishes the entire world. By way of the Kabbalah concerning the word 'the face of the Master,' I have written in the verse וידבר (Exodus 20)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:17.966234529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}